================================================================================
AuraTrace ML Service — Developer Handoff 
================================================================================

OVERVIEW
--------
This is a Python Flask microservice running in Docker that provides 3 AI-powered
endpoints for the AuraTrace Lost & Found system. It handles item matching, storage
prediction, and computer vision item identification.

The ML service is already built, tested, and running. You just need to connect it
to your Laravel system by following the steps below.


================================================================================
THE 3 MODELS
================================================================================

1. BAYESIAN MATCHING MODEL (/match)
------------------------------------
Calculates the probability that a found item belongs to a specific lost report
owner. Uses 3 factors:
  - Category match   (30%) — same category ID = full score, different = 0
  - Zone proximity   (40%) — how close the zones are (hardcoded to 1 for now)
  - Time window      (30%) — how close the dates are within 72 hours

Returns a probability score from 0–100% labeled as:
  - HIGH   (>= 70%)
  - MEDIUM (>= 40%)
  - LOW    (< 40%)

Currently: Runs automatically when a found post is created, matches against all
open lost posts, and returns ranked results in ml_matches in the API response.

Needs: Same logic should also run when a lost post is created — matching against
existing found posts.
(gin try kola ha found post okay man nadara man) (pag integrate mo ini dire dayun maka hatag hin matching probability need pa nim hin code haapp mobile-app/Services/MLService.php)

2. MONTE CARLO SIMULATION (/predict-storage)
---------------------------------------------
Runs 10,000 random simulations to predict when the storage room will reach full
capacity based on:
  - Current item count
  - Total capacity limit
  - Average daily item intake

Returns average days until full + risk level (HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW).

Currently: Endpoint is live and tested. Just needs to be called from the admin
dashboard to display storage capacity alerts.


3. COMPUTER VISION MODEL (/identify)
--------------------------------------
Uses MobileNetV2 (pre-trained on 1000+ object categories) to identify what type
of item is in a photo. Correctly identifies bags, phones, wallets, watches, etc.

Returns:
  - detected item name
  - confidence percentage
  - mapped category_id that matches your database categories
  - top 5 possible detections

Currently: The endpoint works perfectly — tested in Postman, correctly identifies
items from photos.

Needs (one tweak): Laravel currently tries to pass the image URL to Python, but
Python cannot access internal Laravel URLs. The fix is to send the actual image
BYTES directly. The corrected MLService.php code is provided below.


