================================================================================
TIPS FOR THE DEVELOPER
================================================================================

- The ML service is stateless — it does not store anything, just computes
- If /match returns null, the ML service is unreachable — check Docker network
- zone_id is hardcoded to 1 for all posts right now — if you want more accurate
  matching later, add actual zone/building data and pass real zone IDs
- MobileNetV2 works best with clear, well-lit photos
- The category_id returned by /identify maps directly to your categories table
  Make sure your category IDs match the CATEGORY_MAP in vision.py:
    1  = bag / backpack / handbag / purse
    2  = wallet
    3  = cell phone / mobile phone
    4  = book / notebook
    5  = umbrella
    6  = water bottle / bottle
    7  = laptop / computer
    8  = watch / wristwatch
    9  = sunglasses / glasses
    10 = earbuds / headphones / airpods
    11 = id card / card
    12 = key / keys
  If your category IDs are different, update CATEGORY_MAP in vision.py accordingly
- Guzzle is already installed in the Laravel project (verified)
- The ML service auto-restarts on failure (restart: unless-stopped in Docker)


